          "secNumber": "1.2",
          "heading": "Measurement and conservation checkpoints",
          "content": "Write down constituent identities, reinforcement form, interphase treatment, stacking sequence, process history and part geometry; define whether fractions are measured by area, mass or volume; and record the process history that could alter **phase density, fiber form and part-level architecture**. For any local observation, describe why its sampling plan represents the part. Treat **unseen voids or orientation gradients** as an explicit rival explanation and plan **tomography plus representative cross-sectional microscopy** as an independent check.",
